{
  "title": "MIDI Player",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Plays a Standard MIDI",
        "File into whatever",
        "sound generator sits",
        "after it in the slot.",
        "",
        "It is a MIDI FX, so",
        "put it before the",
        "synth in the chain -",
        "it makes no sound of",
        "its own.",
        "",
        "Playback follows",
        "Move's MIDI clock at",
        "24 PPQN, so it starts",
        "and stops with the",
        "transport."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Adding Files",
      "lines": [
        "Upload .mid files to",
        "the module's MIDI",
        "folder, easiest from",
        "Schwung Manager at",
        "move.local:7700.",
        "",
        "They show up in the",
        "slot's preset browser",
        "in alphabetical",
        "order. Jog to one and",
        "click to load it.",
        "",
        "Up to 256 files are",
        "listed.",
        "",
        "There are plenty of",
        "public-domain",
        "classical MIDIs at",
        "mfiles.co.uk."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Controls",
      "lines": [
        "The file list is the",
        "first thing on the",
        "page - jog and click",
        "to choose one.",
        "",
        "Loop",
        " off or on. On by",
        " default: the file",
        " restarts when it",
        " reaches the end.",
        "",
        "Track",
        " opens a list of the",
        " tracks in the file.",
        " Pick one to play it",
        " alone, or take the",
        " merged option to",
        " play all of them",
        " together."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Transport",
      "lines": [
        "Play (Start)",
        " rewinds to the",
        " beginning and plays",
        "Stop",
        " pauses where it is",
        " and sends all notes",
        " off, so nothing",
        " hangs",
        "Continue",
        " resumes from where",
        " it stopped",
        "",
        "The playhead moves on",
        "clock pulses only. If",
        "Move is not running,",
        "nothing plays."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "What Gets Sent",
      "lines": [
        "Notes, pitch bend and",
        "aftertouch pass",
        "through.",
        "",
        "EVERY EVENT IS SENT",
        "ON CHANNEL 1. The",
        "file's own channels",
        "are rewritten, so one",
        "downstream synth",
        "hears the lot. Use",
        "Track to pick a part",
        "rather than expecting",
        "per-channel routing.",
        "",
        "Only these CCs are",
        "passed:",
        " 1   mod wheel",
        " 64  sustain",
        " 66  sostenuto",
        " 67  soft pedal",
        " 123 all notes off",
        "Everything else is",
        "dropped.",
        "",
        "Program changes are",
        "dropped too - the",
        "file cannot pick the",
        "sound. Load the patch",
        "you want in the synth",
        "after it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tempo",
      "lines": [
        "THE FILE'S OWN TEMPO",
        "IS IGNORED.",
        "",
        "Tempo meta events",
        "are discarded on",
        "purpose: playback is",
        "paced by Move's clock,",
        "so a MIDI file always",
        "plays at your project",
        "BPM.",
        "",
        "A file written at 60",
        "BPM and a file at 180",
        "will play at the same",
        "speed. Set the tempo",
        "on the Move.",
        "",
        "Tempo changes inside",
        "a piece are lost for",
        "the same reason."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Limits",
      "lines": [
        "Up to 64 tracks and",
        "65536 events per",
        "file. Larger files",
        "load, but the events",
        "past that are not",
        "played.",
        "",
        "Up to 256 files in",
        "the browser.",
        "",
        "If a file will not",
        "load, check it is a",
        "Standard MIDI File",
        "(.mid) rather than a",
        "karaoke or format-2",
        "variant."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
